  "scope": "Released product merge-plan and group-binding ceilings, static admission, bounded encoding and diagnostic mapping moved to the command adapter. The VM imports the same policy. Frozen plan/group matrices compare both adapter and VM entries without delegating the expected group policy to the migrated wrapper. Four direct adapter tests retain shape/structure/correspondence/size/type order, inclusive encoding bounds and exact diagnostics. A memory VM regression proves refusal before identity reservation, rejection of isolated-member restoration, the original group barrier and first-receipt replay. Group computation, successor construction, capture reentry, journal settlement and recovery authority stay in the VM. Independent native source checkpoint verification is regression evidence, not promotion to a complete host-neutral durable VM. No Linux kernel behavior or GUI packaging changed.",
